    "ruleType": "detachment-rule",
    "group": "Rad-Zone Corps",
    "summary": "**BOMBARDMENT** applies as [battle round](vsdata:core-rule/start-of-battle-round) one opens. For each opposing unit within the opponent’s deployment zone, the opponent chooses whether it stands firm or takes cover. Roll a D6 per unit. **Unit Standing Firm:** That unit takes D3 **[mortal wounds](vsdata:core-rule/mortal-wounds)** if the result reaches 3+. **Unit Taking Cover:** The unit is **battle-shocked**. A 5+ also deals D3 **[mortal wounds](vsdata:core-rule/mortal-wounds)**. Under **FALLOUT**, roll a D6 for every opposing unit in that deployment zone as your [Command phase](vsdata:core-rule/command-phase) opens in battle rounds two through five. A 3+ deals 1 mortal wound and obliges the damaged unit to attempt a [Battle-shock test](vsdata:core-rule/battle-shock).",
